te-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68c179df011c3b7fb8686512_Cursive-Binary_poem-p-800.jpg","Language artist Sasha Stiles’s A LIVING POEM is on view in MoMA’s Gund Lobby from September 10, 2025. The artist speaks with the museum’s Martha Joseph, Associate Curator, Department of Media and Performance and Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["hans-ulrich-obrist-on-exhibitions-as-living-organisms","Hans Ulrich Obrist on Exhibitions as Living Organisms","Peter Bauman","September 1, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68b56b3e75ae7ad1058990a2_Untitled%20design%20(4)-p-800.jpg","Hans Ulrich Obrist spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) about the link between generative art, cybernetics and his do it exhibitions. They discuss how these ideas shaped the famed curator’s more open, evolving approach to his craft."],["hito-steyerl-on-how-it-uses-us","Hito Steyerl on How It Uses Us","Peter Bauman","July 21, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/687e163220133fe94faece5a_Copy%20of%20Winner-p-800.jpg","Artist and theorist Hito Steyerl discusses the material and geopolitical stakes of AI-generated imagery with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["beeple-on-infinite-creation-machines","Beeple on Infinite Creation Machines","Peter Bauman","June 17, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68511b0e2bba85b5cc7f07b3_Screenshot%202025-06-17%20at%209.36.16%20AM-p-800.png","Mike Winkelmann (Beeple) speaks with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) about what motivates the artist—known for his Everydays sketches—to engage with generativity and modern AI’s deep learning tools."],["reprogramming-sensory-habits","Reprogramming Sensory Habits","Luba Elliott","June 9, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68468b1feb7e5fa5fef2eac2_s_Lara%20Hughes%20Install%20(1)-p-800.jpg","Luba Elliott explores what the latest research into AI and creativity reveals about the changing nature of how we see and its impacts on contemporary image making."],["marina-abramovic-on-new-possibilities","Marina Abramović on New Possibilities","Peter Bauman","June 2, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/683d47b1a74c4c26e4e82235_MAE_Octopus%20(2)-p-800.jpg","Marina Abramović’s prolific career spans over six decades of experimentation with performance and audience participation. The storied artist discussed with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) how she's bringing these concepts to the blockchain."],["dmitri-cherniak-on-strictly-for-art","Dmitri Cherniak on Strictly for Art","Peter Bauman","May 26, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68344a2977c3ef0999c74a8d_Dmitri%20Cherniak-p-800.jpg","Dmitri Cherniak is participating in the group show Infinite Images at the Toledo Museum of Art. He discusses the show in a conversation with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony), reflecting on the growing presence of digital and code-based art in museums."],["new-york-city-digital-art-guide","New York City Digital Art Guide","LoVid, Emily Edelman, Josh Yakov, Peter Bauman","May 5, 2025","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6818cc87bbceca179808de17_17-p-800.jpg","Le Random presents a curated guide to New York for digital art lovers, featuring an Art Walk map and highlighting must-see galleries, neighborhoods and artists that define the city’s vibrant digital art scene."],["christiane-paul-on-defining-ai-art","Christiane Paul on Defining AI Art","Peter Bauman","April 23, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6808c18959cf761e585aa1e5_Zurkow%20River%20Is%20a%20Circle-p-800.jpg","Christiane Paul curated the Whitney Museum of American Art's Marina Zurkow: Parting Worlds / Hyundai Terrace Commission: Marina Zurkow. Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) spoke with Paul about the exhibition and how Zurkow’s ecologically attuned practice engages with site specificity."],["the-people-are-in-the-computer--part-i","THE PEOPLE ARE IN THE COMPUTER—PART I","Peter Bauman","March 19, 2025","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/67dad89e0d398ad1157ce216_THE%20PEOPLE%20ARE%20IN%20THE%20COMPUTER-p-800.png","This is the story of Alec Radford, the inventor of ChatGPT, and his foundational contributions to generative AI—a new internet and paradigm for media."],["mario-klingemann-a-i-c-c-a-on-alien-perspective","Mario Klingemann & A.I.C.C.A. on Alien Perspective","Peter Bauman","March 10, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/67cecbe16b9ffe7bfa161485_Screenshot%202025-03-10%20at%2011.18.47%20AM-p-800.jpg","Mario Klingemann, subversive systems artist, and A.I.C.C.A. (Artificially Intelligent Critical Canine), his AI-driven art critic, converse with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["neural-unconscious","Neural Unconscious","Peter Bauman","February 19, 2025","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/67b5de2f24a1436a835b84c2_NU%20square%20logo-p-800.jpg","Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) explores how technology has always changed the way artists see, create and think—first by revealing hidden details (optical unconscious), then by structuring information (computational unconscious) and now by co-generating new possibilities (neural unconscious)."],["barbara-london-on-new-territory","Barbara London on New Territory","Peter Bauman","February 11, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/67ab20dc3518b0f4a29667b6_Jonas-p-800.jpg","Barbara London founded the Museum of Modern Art's (MoMA) video-media exhibition and collection programs in the mid-70s and has played a pivotal role in new media art's shape since then. The curator and author of Video Art/The First Fifty Years (Phaidon: 2020) spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["kim-asendorf-on-elegant-symbiosis","Kim Asendorf on Elegant Symbiosis","Peter Bauman","January 28, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6798b6114063727d59037a9d_Screenshot%202025-01-28%20at%2010.48.13%E2%80%AFAM-p-800.png","Abstract visual artist Kim Asendorf spoke to Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) after the artist's latest release, PXL DEX. The pair discuss the conceptual and technical intricacies of the project, which tokenizes pixels to explore the elegant symbiosis between code, blockchains and culture."],["demystifying-generative-autonomy","Demystifying Generative Autonomy","Peter Bauman","December 12, 2024","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/675ae0ed9a34353550ae3bd4_sougwen-2017_doug2_thumb-p-800.jpg","This is Part IV in a series on building a framework for appreciating generative art. In Part I, “Demystifying Generative Art,” Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) builds the case for such a framework."],["matt-deslauriers-on-a-generative-world","Matt DesLauriers on a Generative World","Peter Bauman","November 19, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6737cacb270614464c52e1a8_bf6-p-800.png","Matt DesLauriers created the generative art project, Bitframes, which serves as a crowdfund for the production of a feature-length documentary film, Generative, providing historical context to generative art. DesLauriers spoke to Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) about both projects."],["sputniko-on-activism-multitasking","Sputniko! on Activism Multitasking","Peter Bauman","November 10, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/67314ce07352ca0c11ed50ef_FC81F341-B852-406A-A852-77CDFA758793-min-p-800.jpg","Artist, designer and entrepreneur Hiromi Ozaki—better known as Sputniko!—recently spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony). The artist and multitasker reflects on digital activism, capitalism’s impact on art and building inclusive systems amidst backlash."],["mat-dryhurst-on-becoming-infinite","Mat Dryhurst on Becoming Infinite","Peter Bauman","October 24, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6719f541954c22fc2bab31ca_677BAA72-9AD0-4476-BF3C-ED4377EDBE8D-p-800.jpg","After visiting Mat Dryhurst and Holly Herndon’s The Call at Serpentine Gallery in London, Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) discussed with Dryhurst the theoretical underpinnings of the duo’s practice, how The Call aligns with this framework and invigorating the AI-data discourse."],["val-ravaglia-on-electric-dreams","Val Ravaglia on Electric Dreams","Peter Bauman","October 17, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6710e6015863eef512e1efb0_Suzanne%20Treister-p-800.jpg","Tate curator Val Ravaglia spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) about their major exhibition, Electric Dreams."],["joan-heemskerk-on-quantum-web4","Joan Heemskerk on Quantum Web4","Peter Bauman","September 10, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/66e00c07bdd7a319df767219_quantq2-p-800.png","Joan Heemskerk of the renowned net.art duo JODI undertook a two-month residency between CERN—the birthplace of the World Wide Web—and Copenhagen Contemporary. The resulting work will be part of a show at Copenhagen Contemporary in 2025."],["then-and-now","THEN AND NOW","Jasia Reichardt","June 25, 2024","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/667a7b47b0b8d8ad5005f86f_JR%20TAN1.png","Cherished icon Jasia Reichardt met with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) before the Foundation Herbert W. Franke's Generative Art Summit Berlin. The Cybernetic Serendipity curator wrote this text as one of the few people who anticipated our digital future along with Franke in the 1960s."],["demystifying-generative-systems","Demystifying Generative Systems","Peter Bauman","June 20, 2024","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/6674137c6f93c64e548bc0c6_ZLHH-p-800.jpeg","This is the third part in a series on building a framework for appreciating generative art. In Part I, “Demystifying Generative Art,” Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) builds the case for such a framework."],["the-algorithmic-gaze-representations-of-women-in-ai-art","The Algorithmic Gaze: Representations of Women in AI Art","Danielle King","June 5, 2024","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/666035db325b1a6beb018d86_Screenshot%202024-06-05%20at%2010.54.28%20AM-p-800.png","Employing John Berger's Ways of Seeing (1974) as a critical lens, Danielle King observes the rise of the algorithmic gaze—the perpetuation of the male gaze into the realm of AI-generated art—underscoring entrenched patriarchal values and the protracted commodification of female bodies."],["demystifying-generative-aesthetics","Demystifying Generative Aesthetics","Peter Bauman","March 21, 2024","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/651c4b639ee9c037fbbbd6c8_Fidenza575-p-800.png","This is the second part in a series on building a framework for appreciating generative art. In the first part, “Demystifying Generative Art,” Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) builds the case for such a framework."],["travess-smalley-profiles-mark-wilson","Travess Smalley Profiles Mark Wilson","Travess Smalley","March 12, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/65f051877c87dafa3700e9ad_e67109_800x800.jpg","Mark Wilson stands as one of digital art's foremost practitioners. Yet as a trained artist, his work is nearly entirely material, demonstrating the delicacy and patience of the painterly, while probing a mechanized, abstract geometric aesthetic."],["lauren-lee-mccarthy-on-software-values","Lauren Lee McCarthy on Software Values","Peter Bauman","February 13, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/65cb645a90c702418d27a1fb_LLM%20SV.jpeg","Lauren Lee McCarthy, celebrated artist, UCLA professor and creator of p5.js, spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) about Seeing Voices, her first long-form generative art project."],["golan-levin-on-the-potentiality-of-blobs","Golan Levin on the Potentiality of Blobs","Peter Bauman","January 10, 2024","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/659da009a13a4b70b20da805_Screenshot%202024-01-09%20at%207.34.44%20PM-min-p-800.png","Artist and educator Golan Levin dips between anecdote and insight with Monk Antony (Peter Bauman), covering Levin's Art Blocks Curated release Cytographia, his drive to unleash the latent capabilities of computers and his role inspiring and promoting open-source art toolkits."],["tyler-hobbs-on-algorithmic-aesthetics","Tyler Hobbs on Algorithmic Aesthetics","Peter Bauman","December 12, 2023","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/656f68737d57eab19bbc0bf2_tyler-hobbs-thin-air-1-2020-med-p-800.jpg","Using the essays of Tyler Hobbs as a reference point, Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) spoke to Hobbs about coded generative art's aesthetics."],["agh-on-glorifying-the-computer","AGH on Glorifying the Computer","Peter Bauman","December 5, 2023","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/64c99287450e318f34a75f08_sv6.svg.png","AGH, the trio of Kim Asendorf, Andreas Gysin and Leander Herzog, spoke with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) before their debut show in Berlin, covering the group's formation, the digital aesthetic and glorifying the computer."],["sougwen-chung-on-us-in-another-form","Sougwen Chung on Us in Another Form","Peter Bauman","October 5, 2023","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/651d7454552d4c520ec7b091_SWC-p-800.png","Multidisciplinary artist Sougwen Chung delves into her unique contributions to the exhibition GEN/GEN: Generative Generations, the evolving discourse on human-machine interconnections and more with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["rhea-myers-on-code-as-cultural-material","Rhea Myers on Code as Cultural Material","Peter Bauman","September 26, 2023","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/651160dab888ea4eb749020a_1-toejectadiskundermacos_1.webp","Artist, hacker and writer, Rhea Myers, discusses her thoughtful contributions to the group exhibition GEN/GEN: Generative Generations and more with Peter Bauman (Monk Antony)."],["zach-lieberman","Zach Lieberman on the Resonance of Generative Art","Peter Bauman","August 2, 2023","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/64ca454a9bd32727847bccd3_Zach%20Lieberman_color%20block%20study-p-800.png","Resonance can refer to qualities of sound and acoustics as well as the power to evoke deep emotions."],["demystifying-generative-art","Demystifying Generative Art","Peter Bauman","July 20, 2023","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/64b80a26a2fd5b2f287e7e39_Screenshot%202023-07-19%20at%205.06.29%20PM-p-800.png","Peter Bauman (Monk Antony) develops a framework for appreciating and analyzing generative art—art using autonomous systems in the vein of Sol LeWitt or Yoko Ono—through an investigation of the movement’s locus of artistic intent."]],"deep":[["the-ultraintelligent-machine-and-gaberbocchus-common-room","The Ultraintelligent Machine and Gaberbocchus Common Room","Jasia Reichardt","September 15, 2025","Article","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68c7d8db08a0af94ec983646_common%20room%203.jpg"],["sasha-stiles-and-martha-joseph-on-language-as-technology","Sasha Stiles and Martha Joseph on Language as Technology","Peter Bauman","September 10, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68c179df011c3b7fb8686512_Cursive-Binary_poem-p-800.jpg"],["hans-ulrich-obrist-on-exhibitions-as-living-organisms","Hans Ulrich Obrist on Exhibitions as Living Organisms","Peter Bauman","September 1, 2025","Interview","https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6411e594fbd274173bf8c35c/68b56b3e75ae7ad1058990a2_Un